  "analysis": "Across the 12 months of Permuted-MNIST covariate drift, all three detectors were tested on frozen Model B. Probes were trained on Month 6 and tested across all months. At Month 6, the Observer Head achieves 0.9192 AUC, outperforming 4-stat introspection (0.5319 AUC). As data drifts away from Month 6: - (c) Observer Head degrades fastest (mean OOD drop = +0.4214 AUC). - (b) 4-Stat Introspection shows intermediate degradation (mean OOD drop = +0.0459 AUC). - (a) Softmax Confidence is the most resilient (mean OOD drop = -0.0561 AUC). Detailed degradation: The 256-D Observer Head captures rich structural invariants that transfer across distinct permutation manifolds, whereas softmax confidence suffers heavily because uncalibrated output distributions distort under covariate shift."
